    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d298">

                <pb facs="0475" n="433" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg433"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 720.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-09-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 22, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> The opening of the campaign is attended
                    with some embarrassments which, in the excitement of the moment, are likely to
                    be exaggerated. The expedition of General Franklin to Sabine Pass was only one
                    of three designed to re-establish the national authority in Texas. Its repulse
                    may retard, but it is not thought that it endangers, the success of the
                    plan.</p>
                <p>Official despatches from the army of the Cumberland have been received of a date
                    so late as two o’clock p.m. of the 21st. They are inexplicit, but their general
                    effect is thought to justify the expectation of our continuing to hold our
                    important positions in Tennessee. Should any later news. be seasonably received,
                    I will communicate it by telegraph.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                    <p>Same to ministers in Europe.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
